{"step_index":198,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:01:37Z","thinking":"**Investigating the Proof Strategy**\n\nExamining `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` to understand the goal. The conjecture relates graph properties. The target is to prove a relationship between radius, and roman domination number.\n```lean\nimport Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nset_option maxRecDepth 10000\n\nopen SimpleGraph\n\n-- Conjecture under test: (nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number\n-- Both declarations refer to the same `Candidate`.\nabbrev Candidate : Prop :=\n    ∀\n```\n\n\n**Examining Relevant Definitions**\n\nExamined the definitions of `GraphCalc.radius G` and `GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G`, expressing them in terms of set operations and the functions `eccentricity`, and `romanWeight`. Focused on the evaluation of `romanDominationNumber` in Lean using `min.getD 0`. The goal is to identify a direct relationship between `radius G` and `romanDominationNumber G`. Considering the definitions of `eccentricity` and `ballWithin`.\n\n\n**Connecting Radius to Roman Weight**\n\nObserved that if a ball of radius $k$ around some vertex covers the entire graph, then the graph's radius is at most $k$. This, in turn, implies radius plus one is less than or equal to $k + 1$.  Hypothesized that if $k + 1$ is less than or equal to the roman weight of a function $f$, then the radius plus one is also less than or equal to the roman weight of $f$.\n\nConsidered if $k$ could be roman weight of $f$ minus one, and looked for a vertex $v$ with ball of radius roman weight $f$ minus one equal to the entire graph. Recalled analyzing this earlier in relation to the eccentricity of vertices. Tested this condition in Python on all connected graphs up to order 6 and found that for every Roman dominating function $f$ there exists such a vertex.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"list_dir","args":{"DirectoryPath":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/.agents\"","toolAction":"\"Analyzing directory\"","toolSummary":"\"List .agents directory\""}}]}
